    buf_bytes(out, "crate::arch::table::INSN_BY_NAME\tjustified\tthe instruction tables' name map, a process-wide static mut the assembler reads; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tfilled only by load_insns, once, on the main thread in the front end before any code generation thread starts (pthread_create orders it before the assembler thread's reads); read-only afterwards\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::arch::table::INSN_FIELDS\tjustified\tthe instruction tables' field offsets, a process-wide static mut the assembler reads; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tpushed only by load_insns, once, on the main thread in the front end before any code generation thread starts; read-only afterwards (insn_text); the IntVec never grows again, so its data never moves under a reader\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::arch::table::INSN_TEXT\tjustified\tthe instruction tables' text, a view the assembler reads through a process-wide static mut; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\twritten only by load_insns (once: it returns when INSN_BUF >= 0), on the main thread in the front end (build -> load_modules -> load_arch_modules) or in volec assemble, before code generation starts any thread (pthread_create orders it before the assembler thread's reads); read-only afterwards (insn_text); the bytes it views are INSN_BUF's buffer's data block, which nothing writes after load_insns (INSN_BUF's only other uses are insn_byte during the load and insn_named's test), and growing BUFS moves the Buf records, not the data block, so the view stays valid for the process\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::back::codecache::FN_IRH\tjustified\tthe code cache's per-function IR hashes, a process-wide static mut every task reads and writes; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tallocated by cc_begin and refilled for every function by cc_phase on the main thread between phases; a task writes only its own functions' entries (out_hash, component_install, scalar_hit); another g's entry is read only through fact(R_IR) in cc_note and reads_hold, after ready_or_done(g) and FN_IRH_OK[g], and an R_IR read of another function is recorded only by inline_call (ir_enter of another runs only on the inliner's unset branches): in the component phase ready_or_done requires g's lower, finished level; outside it the only R_IR reads are -O1 emission's of small leaves, emitted (and so written) only in the next range, after pool_run_joined returned; cleanup and simplify tasks inline nothing, so their entries hold no R_IR of another function\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::back::codecache::FN_IRH_OK\tjustified\tthe code cache's per-function IR-hash validity, a process-wide static mut every task reads and writes; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tas FN_IRH: cc_phase (main, between phases) sets every entry; a task writes only its own (cc_component_begin, cc_emit_begin, cc_scalar_begin, out_hash, component_install, scalar_hit); another g's entry is read only in cc_note and reads_hold for an R_IR read, after ready_or_done(g), and such reads exist only for a lower-level g in the component phase or for an -O1 small leaf whose own emission task runs only in the later range\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::back::codecache::FN_STRS\tjustified\tthe code cache's per-function string lists, a process-wide static mut every task reads and writes; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tcc_phase (main, between phases) refills every entry; a task writes only its own (list_strings(fi) from component_install, out_hash(fi)); another g's list is read (alias_hash, rel_sources, get_tables) only for g in the task's R_IR reads (cc.reads, read_irs), which passed ready_or_done and FN_IRH_OK: a lower, finished level in the component phase, or an -O1 small leaf in emission, whose list no task writes during emission\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::back::codecache::OUT_COMP\tjustified\tthe code cache's per-component outcome, a process-wide static mut; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tallocated by cc_begin on the main thread before the phases; written only at the component's first function's index by that component's task (cc_component_begin, cc_component_end: scc_order[start]); read only by report on the main thread at cc_end, after the phases and parallel_end\n");
