    buf_bytes(out, "crate::back::codecache::OUT_SCALAR\tjustified\tthe code cache's per-function scalar outcome, a process-wide static mut; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tallocated by cc_begin on the main thread; OUT_SCALAR[fi] written only by fi's cleanup/simplify task (cc_scalar_begin, cc_scalar_end); read only by report at cc_end\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::back::codecache::SCALAR_REC\tjustified\tthe code cache's per-function scalar recordings, a process-wide static mut; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tallocated by cc_begin on the main thread; entry fi reached only through scalar_rec(fi) by fi's own task: cc_scalar_begin and cc_scalar_cleanup_end in its cleanup task, cc_scalar_simplify_begin and scalar_hit in its simplify task a phase later (phases ordered by MUTEX); one task per function per phase\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::back::codecache::pack::NEW\tjustified\tthe code cache pack's new entries, a process-wide static mut; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tallocated by pack_load on the main thread before the phases; slot s = SLOTS_PER_FN * fi + kind - 1 written only by pack_new from store, called by the task for fi and that kind (cc_component_end for scc_order[start], cc_emit_end, cc_scalar_end), so each slot has one writer; pack_changed/pack_save read it on the main thread after the phases\n");
    buf_bytes(out, "crate::back::codecache::pack::USED\tjustified\tthe code cache pack's used marks, a process-wide static mut; Rust has no safe access to a static mut\tallocated by pack_load on the main thread; since 0.27.8 a task marks USED[e] (mark_used, mark_used_fn) only when none of its functions is fn_ambig; e is the entry whose 128-bit key (a, b) equals the task's exactly (pack_find); a key mixes each member's fn_nameh, and names_begin marks fn_ambig every function whose name key another shares, so two marking tasks of one phase have distinct key inputs (one IR function per front function: ir_new_func's only caller is lower_body), and the same e only if two distinct inputs hash to the same 128-bit key, which the cache already assumes never happens (such a hit would also install the wrong code); phases are ordered by MUTEX; pack_changed and pack_save read it on the main thread after the phases\n");
